[Music]  the prize are for a loved one she'll  never see again  others console her they were here in Moo  Levi killed ten years ago fleeing heavy  and indiscriminate shelling they were  forced onto a tiny patch of land with  nowhere to go  many were separated from their families  as they fled my husband went missing we  were on in different directions I ran  with my children one way my husband went  in another we didn't see each other  after that I tell my children their  father is alive and he'll come home one  day but in my heart I think he's gone I  think he died music plays as mourners  light flames for those who died the UN  says some 40,000 people were killed in  mere weeks other reports indicate the  death toll is much much higher some  survivors saw family members perish  before their eyes unable to forget what  they witnessed they're desperate to  remember a relative these girls were  orphaned here a decade ago sister  Krishan II helps care for children  without parents she says even the very  young remain traumatized they remember  they remember the path their families  took as they fled they remember being in  a place where so many died they remember  parents and the children wanted to come  here now one of the girls didn't want to  in the past thinking about her father  but wanted to be here today  the moles have come to this remembrance  event from all across the country  there's sorrow but there's also a sense  of guilt  everyone has dreams I've studied I have  a job but the people who died here had  dreams too and that's devastating I'm  living my life they lost theirs they say  it's up to them to memorialize their  dead four thumb holes in Sri Lanka the  grief is shared the pain still raw

